# Cubic and quadratic residue waves
# A moving target reveals finite-field level sets hidden inside x³ + y².

:mim 1

:param target number = 0
:vary target from 0 to 31 over 12s loop

:axis x integers
:axis y integers

# Keep the polynomial fixed so its geometry remains stable through time.
:field mod(x * x * x + y * y, 31)

# Measure circular distance from each residue to the moving target.
# Invert the distance so the selected modular level set glows brightest.
:lens 15.5 - min(mod(value - target, 31), mod(target - value, 31))

:color magnitude(lens)
:overlay equality off
